  "inputBoundary": "One caller-supplied finite speed in kilometers per hour for a location reading. The paper derives speed from distance and elapsed time between the previous and current location points; ordering, first-row handling, distance calculation, and timestamp normalization remain upstream.",
  "outputBoundary": "Retain readings with speed strictly below 5 km/h as stationary and exclude readings at or above 5 km/h as moving.",
  "limitations": [
    "The separate accuracy filter that discards readings with more than 50 meters accuracy is not part of this setting.",
    "The source discloses the strict stationary comparator but not coordinate-distance formula, ordering tie behavior, zero or negative elapsed-time handling, or first-row disposition; those operations remain upstream and unresolved.",
    "A missing or nonfinite speed fails closed before classification; no rounding, tolerance, or physical speed range is invented.",
    "Significant-place clustering, the 200-meter centroid rule, centroid updates, place ranking, coder ratings, and downstream notification/app analyses are outside this setting."
